*> Implementation test of SEED-FROM-TEXT (T0336; docs/protocol/11 section 12): the text of CS-SEED-TEXT
*> (PIC X(64), UTF-8, space padded) becomes the world seed: trim (code units up to 0x20), empty = random,
*> else a base-10 signed 64-bit number (also Unicode decimal digits, optional + or -), else the 32-bit Java
*> string hash of the UTF-16 units sign-extended. Every worked example of section 12.4 is a case here.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-SEED-TEXT.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 01 WS-TEXT                PIC X(64).
 01 WS-SEED                BINARY-DOUBLE.
 01 WS-RANDOM              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-SEED-2              BINARY-DOUBLE.
 01 WS-RANDOM-2            BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-EDIT                PIC -(19)9.
 01 WS-RANDOM-EDIT         PIC 9.
 01 WS-EXPECT              PIC X(40).
 01 WS-TAB                 PIC X VALUE X"09".
 01 WS-LF                  PIC X VALUE X"0A".
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-TEXT
     MOVE "row 1 empty text is no seed" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "1" TO WS-EXPECT
     PERFORM CHECK-RANDOM

     MOVE "   " TO WS-TEXT
     MOVE "row 2 three spaces are no seed" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "1" TO WS-EXPECT
     PERFORM CHECK-RANDOM

     MOVE "empty text gives a random seed: two draws differ" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-TEXT
     CALL "SEED-FROM-TEXT" USING WS-TEXT WS-SEED WS-RANDOM
     CALL "SEED-FROM-TEXT" USING WS-TEXT WS-SEED-2 WS-RANDOM-2
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF WS-SEED NOT = WS-SEED-2 AND WS-RANDOM = 1 AND WS-RANDOM-2 = 1
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

     MOVE "12345" TO WS-TEXT MOVE "row 3 number" TO TL-CASE MOVE "0 12345" TO WS-EXPECT PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE "-42" TO WS-TEXT MOVE "row 4 negative number" TO TL-CASE MOVE "0 -42" TO WS-EXPECT PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE "  42  " TO WS-TEXT MOVE "row 5 trim then number" TO TL-CASE MOVE "0 42" TO WS-EXPECT PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE "+5" TO WS-TEXT MOVE "row 6 plus sign" TO TL-CASE MOVE "0 5" TO WS-EXPECT PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE "007" TO WS-TEXT MOVE "row 7 leading zeros" TO TL-CASE MOVE "0 7" TO WS-EXPECT PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE "-0" TO WS-TEXT MOVE "row 8 minus zero" TO TL-CASE MOVE "0 0" TO WS-EXPECT PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE "9223372036854775807" TO WS-TEXT MOVE "row 9 upper bound" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "0 9223372036854775807" TO WS-EXPECT PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE "-9223372036854775808" TO WS-TEXT MOVE "row 10 lower bound" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "0 -9223372036854775808" TO WS-EXPECT PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE "9223372036854775808" TO WS-TEXT MOVE "row 11 one above the bound is hashed" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "0 -1773151197" TO WS-EXPECT PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE "-9223372036854775809" TO WS-TEXT MOVE "row 12 one below the bound is hashed" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "0 1304595159" TO WS-EXPECT PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE "12345678901234567890" TO WS-TEXT MOVE "row 13 too long is hashed" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "0 -1902336138" TO WS-EXPECT PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE "-" TO WS-TEXT MOVE "row 14 lone sign is hashed" TO TL-CASE MOVE "0 45" TO WS-EXPECT PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE "hello" TO WS-TEXT MOVE "row 15 hash" TO TL-CASE MOVE "0 99162322" TO WS-EXPECT PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE "  hello  " TO WS-TEXT MOVE "row 16 trim then hash" TO TL-CASE MOVE "0 99162322" TO WS-EXPECT PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE "a b" TO WS-TEXT MOVE "row 17 inner space is hashed" TO TL-CASE MOVE "0 94307" TO WS-EXPECT PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE "1.5" TO WS-TEXT MOVE "row 18 decimal point is hashed" TO TL-CASE MOVE "0 48568" TO WS-EXPECT PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE "0x10" TO WS-TEXT MOVE "row 19 hex is hashed" TO TL-CASE MOVE "0 1546855" TO WS-EXPECT PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE "-+5" TO WS-TEXT MOVE "row 20 minus plus is hashed" TO TL-CASE MOVE "0 44631" TO WS-EXPECT PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE "++5" TO WS-TEXT MOVE "row 21 plus plus is hashed" TO TL-CASE MOVE "0 42709" TO WS-EXPECT PERFORM CHECK

     MOVE SPACES TO WS-TEXT
     STRING FUNCTION CHAR(227) FUNCTION CHAR(137) FUNCTION CHAR(147) "5" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-TEXT
     MOVE "row 22 U+2212 then 5 is hashed" TO TL-CASE MOVE "0 270435" TO WS-EXPECT PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-TEXT
     STRING FUNCTION CHAR(218) FUNCTION CHAR(164) FUNCTION CHAR(218) FUNCTION CHAR(165)
         DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-TEXT
     MOVE "row 23 Arabic-Indic 3 and 4 are digits" TO TL-CASE MOVE "0 34" TO WS-EXPECT PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-TEXT
     STRING FUNCTION CHAR(196) FUNCTION CHAR(170) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-TEXT
     MOVE "row 24 e acute is one unit 233" TO TL-CASE MOVE "0 233" TO WS-EXPECT PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-TEXT
     STRING FUNCTION CHAR(241) FUNCTION CHAR(160) FUNCTION CHAR(153) FUNCTION CHAR(129)
         DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-TEXT
     MOVE "row 25 U+1F600 is two units" TO TL-CASE MOVE "0 1772899" TO WS-EXPECT PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-TEXT
     STRING WS-TAB "7" WS-LF DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-TEXT
     MOVE "row 26 tab and line feed are trimmed" TO TL-CASE MOVE "0 7" TO WS-EXPECT PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE "Hello World" TO WS-TEXT MOVE "row 27 Hello World" TO TL-CASE MOVE "0 -862545276" TO WS-EXPECT PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE "The quick brown fox" TO WS-TEXT MOVE "row 28 The quick brown fox" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "0 -1739336029" TO WS-EXPECT PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE "North Carolina" TO WS-TEXT MOVE "row 29 North Carolina" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "0 -343522682" TO WS-EXPECT PERFORM CHECK
     STOP RUN.

 CHECK.
     CALL "SEED-FROM-TEXT" USING WS-TEXT WS-SEED WS-RANDOM
     MOVE WS-RANDOM TO WS-RANDOM-EDIT
     MOVE WS-SEED TO WS-EDIT
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE WS-EXPECT TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-RANDOM-EDIT) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT.

 CHECK-RANDOM.
     CALL "SEED-FROM-TEXT" USING WS-TEXT WS-SEED WS-RANDOM
     MOVE WS-RANDOM TO WS-RANDOM-EDIT
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE WS-EXPECT TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-RANDOM-EDIT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT.
 END PROGRAM TEST-SEED-TEXT.
